From: Orange Pi 5B Builder <pencil.bsp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:30:00 +0700
Subject: panvk: answer the v2 DRM format modifier query

panvk_GetPhysicalDeviceFormatProperties2() fills
VkDrmFormatModifierPropertiesListEXT but ignores
VkDrmFormatModifierPropertiesList2EXT, so the 2 form always comes back with a
count of zero. panvk advertises VK_KHR_format_feature_flags2, which is what
makes the 2 form valid to ask for, so a caller has every reason to use it.

Six other Mesa Vulkan drivers -- radv, anv, v3dv, nvk, hk -- answer both.

A caller that asks only the 2 way concludes the GPU supports no modifiers at
all. gnome-remote-desktop 50 does exactly that: it skips the GPU with "No DRM
format modifiers available for DRM format 875713112", skips the software
rasterizer for want of the extension, acquires no physical device, and quietly
encodes H.264 on the CPU with nothing in the log to say the hardware encoder
was passed over.

The two queries differ only in the width of the feature mask -- v1 carries
VkFormatFeatureFlags, v2 carries VkFormatFeatureFlags2 -- so enumerate the
modifiers once and let each list copy what it can hold. v1 keeps its 32-bit
truncation, which is what it has always done.

Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-09-14
